Read mining and mineral engineering from ordinary material questions to independent investigation (@mine-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "A-mine-and-material-question.lingua#r_694Z4QKSQX4N53DXACCKKG0G0M") { r_2Z1REVC9436XNDEFSV6C9PX04S
**Read:** [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the entire course as the first sustained reading; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the complete handbook during the mining progression; [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete sixth edition during the processing progression.

Begin with the following material question and read the whole Penn State MNG 230 course in parallel with the first pass through these Records. Start from material, quantity, maps, observations, and what a mine/plant does. Use [Quantitative and technical literacy](../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2), [Measurement and metrology](../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../../../../gaia/earth/geology/Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06), [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../../../../gaia/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN), and [General chemistry](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V) at the point where a concept is unfamiliar; their complete programmes remain available without making every neighboring subject an entry barrier.

Read the whole Hard Rock Miner's Handbook and the full public NPTEL surface and underground courses during method, layout, ground, equipment, and operation study. Derive and work the examples rather than memorizing isolated rules. Read Hoek and McPherson in full as the ground and service systems deepen. Government manuals supply complete applicable field/design methods with their actual domains and dates.

For processing, read all twenty CETEM Tratamento de Minérios chapters, the full Práticas Laboratoriais manual, the complete NPTEL processing sequence, and the entire Usinas casebook. English and Portuguese sources can be used together. Read the full environmental/closure handbooks and assigned primary papers. Wills, Principles of Mineral Processing, and the SME handbook provide optional authorized professional comparisons; the freely accessible spine remains substantial.

The later sustained studies require derivations, independent balance/model checks, whole published cases, competing designs, uncertainty, and original scholarly investigation. State what was actually performed in laboratory/field settings and what was investigated through literature or supplied data. Specific later readings narrow to an equation, method, or set of observations after the whole source supplies context. All books, articles, lectures, models, and external data remain at their authorized sources; these Records provide original explanations, examples, work, and connections.

**Continue:** [Begin with a material need and the evidence connecting it with a mine](A-mine-and-material-question.lingua#r_694Z4QKSQX4N53DXACCKKG0G0M).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
